### Bug description

## Summary

In `processProximityPacket`, the spectator branch fails to `return` when neither `spectator_player_possession` nor `spectator_interaction` is enabled. As a result, the spectator's voice falls through to the regular proximity broadcast and is sent to every nearby player as a `PlayerSoundPacket` — exactly as if the player were not in spectator mode.

Both default configs are `false`, so this affects every server out of the box.

## Affected code

`common/src/main/java/de/maxhenkel/voicechat/voice/server/Server.java` (Fabric / Forge / NeoForge / Quilt), lines 419-446:

```java
if (sender.isSpectator()) {
    if (Voicechat.SERVER_CONFIG.spectatorPlayerPossession.get()) {
        // ... handles possession case, returns if camera is a player
    }
    if (Voicechat.SERVER_CONFIG.spectatorInteraction.get()) {
        soundPacket = new LocationSoundPacket(...);
        source = SoundPacketEvent.SOURCE_SPECTATOR;
    }
    // BUG: no return / no else — falls through below when both configs are false
}

if (soundPacket == null) {
    soundPacket = new PlayerSoundPacket(...);   // spectator gets broadcast as a normal player
    source = SoundPacketEvent.SOURCE_PROXIMITY;
}

broadcast(ServerWorldUtils.getPlayersInRange(...), soundPacket, sender, senderState, groupId, source);
```

The same bug exists in `bukkit/src/main/java/de/maxhenkel/voicechat/voice/server/Server.java` lines 353-394 (Bukkit / Paper).

## Notes

- Group chat is unaffected — `processGroupPacket` is called separately and does not consult spectator state, which is the intended behavior.
- Discovered on branch `26.1`.

PR follows.

### Minecraft version

1.21.11

### Mod/Plugin version

latest default branch (1ba180c)

### Mod/Plugin loader and version

Feather 2.6.13-c

### Steps to reproduce


1. Use any server with default config (`spectator_interaction = false`, `spectator_player_possession = false`).
2. Player A switches to spectator mode and flies near Player B.
3. Player A speaks — Player B hears them.



### Expected behavior

Expected: Player A is silent to Player B since `spectator_interaction = false`.


